 "draw": "<!-- jackioh-bot:card-sets -->\n### 🃏 Which set's cards win most\n\n_Read at 2026-09-29 12:00 from production's card statistics (`/api/stats/cards`), once a day: the last 3 patches with 1,000 games or more, v0.4.2 (1,200 live games), v0.4.0 (1,100 live and AI games) and v0.3.5 (1,500 live games)._\n\n| Set | Cards | Card-games | Pooled | Mean | Median | v0.4.2 | v0.4.0 | v0.3.5 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Core | 1 | 3,800 | 52.6% ±0.8 | 52.6% | 52.6% | 58.3% | 50.0% | 50.0% |\n| Classic | 2 | 3,810 | 48.7% ±0.8 | 48.7% | 48.7% | 45.0% | 50.0% | 50.7% |\n\nHighest pooled: **Core**; mean: **Core**; median: **Core**.\n\n<details><summary>Cards 3 or more standard errors from 50% (1)</summary>\n\n| Card | Set | Win rate | Games | z |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Stockpile (`core-001`) | Core | 52.6% | 3,800 | +3.2 |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>A card's win rate is its deck's, over the games it was in a deck (R377); a set's pooled rate is its cards' wins over their games, its mean and median over the cards with 20 games or more. Decks mix sets, so this is how a set's cards fare in mixed decks. ± is one standard error as if every card-game were independent, which they are not, so sets less than two or three ± apart are within noise.</sub>\n\n<!-- /jackioh-bot:card-sets -->",
